From 8d0342f16f72533c9d78b612b209020114de26fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Hertenberger <erde74@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:14:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] plan9: cgo on arm64; notes and exit with threads of C's
 own

- arm64: load_g and save_g for plan9 (tls_arm64.s): with cgo g is also in
  APE's _privates[1] (C may use R28 between saving and restoring it);
  sigtramp loads it in a cgo program. The heap segment at 8 GB: 9front's
  arm64 user space is 32 GB, a segment at most 8 GB.
- cmd/go, debug/plan9obj: 9front's arm64 a.out magic (cmd/go would not
  overwrite a plan9/arm64 program it took for no object).
- A note on a proc without g (a thread of C's own in a cgo program) is
  left alone (badnote: noted NCONT; a trap of its own the default) instead
  of ending that thread; the runtime's threads get a note to the note
  group themselves.
- exit in a cgo program has APE end its pthreads (x_cgo_exitall):
  threads of C's own kept running after main returned. goexitsall first,
  so that an m made meanwhile ends in minit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
